// expect: 42
// A pipe stage whose callee's arrow is not yet known is the product the
// Stage Law reads: its arguments, then the piped value. `frame`'s record is
// an unannotated parameter, so `rig.tone`'s type is learned from this one
// use, and `2 |> rig.tone(40)` makes it `(Int, Int) -> Int`, the stage built
// below. Until 2026-10-06 the stage was judged as a complete call returning
// a function, the field read `(Int) -> (Int) -> Int`, and the call into
// `frame` refused a correct program with an arity mismatch.
fn add(a, b) = a + b

fn build() = {tone: add}

fn frame(rig) = 2 |> rig.tone(40)

fn main() = frame(build())
